# Matplotlib defaults to Type 3 fonts in PDF and EPS. Type 3 is a bitmapped glyph
# program: the text cannot be searched or copied reliably, some viewers render it
# poorly at small sizes, and Elsevier's artwork guidance asks for embedded TrueType
# or Type 1. An AE review pass found Type 3 faces in seventeen submitted figures.
#
# scripts/_figstyle.py sets the same two keys, but only for generators that call
# set_style(). Several power-sector and sensitivity figures build their own axes
# without it, so the setting lives here as well: matplotlib reads matplotlibrc from
# the working directory, and every generator runs with cwd=code.
#
# 42 is TrueType. The figures are otherwise unchanged.
pdf.fonttype: 42
ps.fonttype:  42
